{"id":"jarmuth","name":"Jarmuth","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:jarmuth"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Jarmuth","text":"Height. (1.) A town in the plain of Judah (Josh. 15:35), originally the residence of one of the Canaanitish kings (10:3, 5, 23). It has been identified with the modern Yarmuk, a village about 7 miles north-east of Beit-Jibrin. (2.) A Levitical city of the tribe of Issachar (Josh. 21:29), supposed by some to be the Ramah of Samuel (1 Sam. 19:22)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3412","lemma":"יַרְמוּת","xlit":"Yarmûwth","gloss":"Jarmuth, the name of two places in Palestine","kjv":"Jarmuth","count":7,"share":1},{"strong":"H3923","lemma":"לָכִישׁ","xlit":"Lâkîysh","gloss":"Lakish, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Lachish","count":4,"share":0.57},{"strong":"H5700","lemma":"עֶגְלוֹן","xlit":"ʻEglôwn","gloss":"Eglon, the name of a place in Palestine and of a Moabiti","kjv":"Eglon","count":3,"share":0.43},{"strong":"H2275","lemma":"חֶבְרוֹן","xlit":"Chebrôwn","gloss":"Chebron, a place in Palestine, also the name of two Isra","kjv":"Hebron","count":3,"share":0.43},{"strong":"H2568","lemma":"חָמֵשׁ","xlit":"châmêsh","gloss":"five","kjv":"fif, fifth, five","count":2,"share":0.29}],"verses":["Josh.10.3","Josh.10.5","Josh.10.23","Josh.12.11","Josh.15.35","Josh.21.29","Neh.11.29"],"related":[{"id":"adoni-zedek","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.097,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"debir","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.079,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"hebron","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.033,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"azekah","type":"lexical","strong":"H3923","why":"both lead with לָכִישׁ (H3923)"},{"id":"lachish","type":"lexical","strong":"H3923","why":"both lead with לָכִישׁ (H3923)"}],"works":[]}
